Subject: Set Tape's regtest halving interval to 210000 blocks
Base: Bitcoin Core v30.4

Tape's regtest network uses the same 210000-block subsidy halving interval
as mainnet. The interval is a consensus rule: block data must be validated
with the same interval under which it was created.

diff --git a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
--- a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
@@ -519,7 +519,7 @@
         m_chain_type = ChainType::REGTEST;
         consensus.signet_blocks = false;
         consensus.signet_challenge.clear();
-        consensus.nSubsidyHalvingInterval = 150;
+        consensus.nSubsidyHalvingInterval = 210000;
         consensus.BIP34Height = 1; // Always active unless overridden
         consensus.BIP34Hash = uint256();
         consensus.BIP65Height = 1;  // Always active unless overridden
